  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 427 AM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nCurrent surface analysis places cold front stretching through\nthe upper Midwest into the central plains, while high pressure\nsettles over the northern plains. Upper level analysis places\ntrough stretching through eastern Manitoba, with ridge off the\nwest coast. Quiet weather remains over our area in the wake of\na front and affiliated wave that moved through last night\nbringing some precipitation to parts of the area.\n\nFor today, a cooler and dry day is on tap in the wake of the\naforementioned cold front with most locations only pushing into\nthe lower to mid 70s, which is about 10 to 15 degrees below\naverage.\n\nWarmer air then starts to work into the area through mid-week\nresulting in a warming trend bringing temperatures back up to\nnear to a bit above average. Mainly dry conditions are expected\nthrough this period, though a weak disturbance moving through\nmay bring a light shower or storm to the Turtle Mountains and\nsurrounding area. \n\nSeasonal temperatures then continue through the weekend into\nearly next week. Dry weather also continues going into the\nweekend, with some low to medium (20 to 40 percent) chances for\nprecipitation developing early next week.",
